WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.500
To get the most out of what's set to be one
of the biggest, most unmissable blockbusters

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.910
of the summer and possibly the year, we've
rounded up the tidbits and plot details you'll

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:09.680
want to brush up on.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.480
Here's everything you need to know before
you see Fast and Furious Presents: Hobbs and

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.020
Shaw.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.920
When the character is first introduced in
Fast Five, Johnson's Agent Luke Hobbs is a

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.500
straitlaced do-gooder in the Diplomatic Security
Service.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.710
As a result, he spends the majority of that
movie tracking down Vin Diesel's Dominic Toretto

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.620
in a bid to stop Dom and his crew from pulling
off the most outlandish heist Rio has ever

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.160
seen.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.140
But it's not long before Hobbs grudgingly
sees the good in the gang, and decides to

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:36.920
work with them.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.180
The vault of money they're heisting belongs
to drug lord Hernan Reyes, who is so peeved

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.650
about his profits getting plundered that he
kills Hobbs' entire team and attempts to frame

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.080
Toretto and his gang for the hit.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.520
But Hobbs is smarter than the average beefcake
and collaborates with the Fast crew to get

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.420
even with Reyes.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:57.100
Fast Five marked the beginning of a fruitful
relationship between Hobbs and Toretto's gang,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.140
with Hobbs growing to understand the complicated
gray area between being a good guy and a bad

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:01.660
guy.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.000
Here's where the soap opera leanings of the
Fast and Furious franchise really start going

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.800
into overdrive.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:12.600
When Hobbs returns in Fast and Furious 6,
he teams up with the gang again to take down

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.820
terrorist Owen Shaw.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.220
Shaw ends up in a coma after his battle with
the Fast Family, but there's also a twist

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.140
ending which introduces Jason Statham as Owen's
brother, Deckard Shaw.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.460
A post-credits scene reveals that he was behind
team member Han's death in The Fast and Furious:

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:27.980
Tokyo Drift.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.100
Although Tokyo Drift is the third film of
the franchise, it takes place between the

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.600
events of Fast &amp; Furious 6 and Furious 7.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:39.259
Deckard continues as the baddie in Furious
7, but he's grudgingly forced to make nice

00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:42.619
with the Fast gang to get even with the big
bad in Fate of the Furious.

00:01:42.619 --> 00:01:46.540
Still, even by the end of the film, Shaw is
pretty clear about the fact that none of his

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:50.300
baby-saving action scenes made him a willing
member of Toretto's "family."

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:52.700
"I can't believe you went to see my mother."

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.520
That makes him the perfect foil for Hobbs.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.960
One of the biggest reasons Hobbs and Shaw
have such an entertaining dynamic is that

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.520
they have complementary character arcs within
the series.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.630
While Hobbs has realized that he sometimes
has to break a few laws and collaborate with

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:13.940
criminals to save the day, Shaw has discovered
that he sometimes needs the help of good guys

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.320
to carry out his dirty deeds.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.640
Their conflicting sets of morals and goals
has given them one of the most fascinating

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.980
and hilarious relationships in the franchise.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.400
As highlighted by the prison break scene from
the Fate of the Furious, these two rivals

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.580
are often forced to fight alongside each other
while also fighting against each other.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:34.280
Speaking to IGN, director David Leitch has
copped to the fact that Hobbs and Shaw was

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.840
influenced by the buddy cop movies he grew
up loving:

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:43.600
"There's these buddy movies from the '80s
and '90s like Lethal Weapon and 48 Hours that

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.960
really speak to me as a filmmaker."

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:50.160
If you've caught even just five minutes of
a Fast and Furious movie, then you already

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.800
know just how important family is to the franchise.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.180
"I don't have friends.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.320
I got family."

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.910
Not only is it Toretto's favorite word and
motive for committing crimes, but those family

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.250
values also provide the backbone for much
of the franchise's major plots.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:09.360
Hobbs and Shaw looks to be extending these
values from the franchise to the spinoff,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:09.880
too.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.700
Not only is noted Fast and Furious superfan
Helen Mirren returning to play Shaw's rough-and-ready

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.500
mother, but his sister, played by Vanessa
Kirby, is also showing up as a main character.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:25.260
Hattie Shaw, an MI-5 agent, looks to be bringing
some serious trouble in Hobbs and Shaw's direction.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.590
She'll be appealing to Shaw's loyalty to family
and Hobbs' loyalty to saving the world in

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.780
taking down Idris Elba's villainous Brixton.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.280
But it isn't just Shaw's brood that'll be
a major part of the movie.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.140
Though we haven't seen much of Hobbs' family
in the franchise so far, it looks as though

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.880
Hobbs and Shaw will be introducing audiences
to Hobbs' full Samoan family.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:47.740
The most recent trailer for the movie teases
a massive set piece involving Hobbs' family,

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:51.510
who look like they'll be putting their traditional
fighting skills to good use in helping their

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.060
brother defeat Brixton's endless squad of
bad guys.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.140
Interestingly, the family connection doesn't
end there: Johnson's cousin, WWE wrestler

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:03.500
Roman Reigns, will be swinging a sledgehammer
of family justice as Hobbs' brother.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.840
Speaking to Empire, Leitch has teased great
things for the battle sequence, particularly

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.140
for fans of a good old-fashioned smackdown.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:14.530
"Roman Reigns and Dwayne teaming up as sort
of a tag team against a couple of mercenaries

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:15.420
is pretty awesome.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.880
It's going to be a huge treat for wrestling
fans."

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.240
Bringing a new villainous dimension to the
Fast and Furious franchise, and adding to

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.560
the already stellar roster of actors in the
series, is Idris Elba as Brixton.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.720
The self-proclaimed "black Superman" looks
to be one of the most powerful foes Hobbs

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.400
and Shaw have encountered thus far.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:34.320
"Damn.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.260
He really is black Superman."

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.420
Described in the official plot description
as a "cyber-genetically enhanced anarchist,"

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:45.520
Brixton is a supervillain who appears to be
abusing technology to make himself harder,

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.259
bigger, faster, stronger.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.520
Oh, and it looks like he's bulletproof to
boot.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:54.349
With trailers for Hobbs and Shaw showing the
villain using technology to bulk up and hulk

00:04:54.349 --> 00:04:58.490
out while also threatening the world with
an insidious bio-threat, Brixton promises

00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:59.840
to be a next-level heavy.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.720
Asked by Collider whether he wanted to build
a whole new world of characters for Hobbs

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:09.500
and Shaw or borrow some familiar faces from
the franchise, Leitch sounds like he's open

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.780
to the idea of cameos:

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:15.780
"I think it' be fun to nod and have a couple
of the characters come by and make their appearances.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:19.560
But I think we have a really strong point
of view that we want to create our own characters

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.560
for this world."

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.509
That certainly sounds like the answer of a
man holding his cards close to the vest, as

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:25.509
he should be.

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:28.979
Surprise cameos of this nature always work
best when they're at their most unexpected.

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:33.050
Still, we perhaps shouldn't rule out a brief
surprise appearance from beloved characters

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:36.930
like Ludacris' Tej Parker or Tyrese Gibson's
Roman Pearce.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.740
However, the greatest and most unexpected
cameo may come from someone outside the existing

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.440
Fast family.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:47.440
Keanu Reeves was rumored to make an appearance
in the film, but unfortunately The Rock himself

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:52.040
shot down that much-anticipated cameo in a
conversation with MTV News, saying:

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.370
"I will confirm that he's not in it, by the
way.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.120
That rumor just started to kind of swell.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.820
But I will tell you this, we do have some
surprises coming."

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.979
Just what those surprises could be is anyone's
guess.

00:06:01.979 --> 00:06:03.630
Could it be the return of Han?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.720
A surprise casting for a Shaw patriarch?

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:10.480
Or could The Rock just be blowing a smokescreen
to make the Keanu cameo hit even harder?

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.180
Don't get your hopes up for a cameo appearance
from Vin Diesel in Hobbs and Shaw, though,

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.700
not even at the traditional post-action barbecue.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.659
Not only is Hobbs and Shaw looking to establish
its own cinematic universe without Toretto,

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.800
but there's still the alleged beef between
Diesel and Johnson to deal with.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:31.540
That beef surfaced in August 2016 during the
last week of filming Fate of the Furious,

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:35.680
when Johnson published a cryptic Instagram
post which implied that an anonymous co-star

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:39.900
wasn't conducting himself as a, quote, "true
professional" and that fans could see his

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.400
blood, quote, "legit boiling" in some scenes.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:47.580
The feud seemed to drag on for months under
the guise of vague social media back-and-forths,

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:49.600
with Michelle Rodriguez even confirming it
to People:

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:50.700
“They’re ‘bros,’ man.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.440
They’re friends, and ultimately even friends
reach a point where they have to set aside

00:06:54.449 --> 00:06:58.860
their differences to make a movie for multicultural
people around the world, and that is the bigger

00:06:58.860 --> 00:06:59.600
scheme of things.”

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:03.960
The two have since reportedly buried the hatchet,
with Johnson telling Entertainment Tonight

00:07:03.979 --> 00:07:06.129
that he and Diesel are simply different people:

00:07:06.129 --> 00:07:10.560
"Just like, in life, you have different philosophies
and people have different fundamental philosophies

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.020
on how you do things."

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.540
Meanwhile, Diesel said of his co-star:

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:14.800
"We still love each other.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.340
That's my boy."

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:20.740
The Fast and Furious franchise has built a
reputation for itself as one of the boldest,

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:24.080
most ridiculous, and bombastic action film
series ever made.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.520
With Leitch directing Hobbs and Shaw and regular
Fast and Furious writer Chris Morgan behind

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:32.330
the screenplay, the spinoff looks as though
it's in capable hands for maintaining that

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:32.860
reputation.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.640
Not only did Morgan pen the first film, he's
also the man behind the genius resurgence

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.920
of the franchise from Fast Five onwards.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.720
He's the writer who looked at the ludicrously
giant action sequences already delivered by

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.500
the franchise and said, "No, let's go bigger."

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:51.460
"Start out stealing DVD players in East LA
and ends up stealing 100 million dollars in

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:52.060
Rio."

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.080
"Not bad, huh?"

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:58.900
Meanwhile, Leitch might be one of Hollywood's
most highly sought after and respected action

00:07:58.900 --> 00:07:59.460
directors.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:03.220
The former stuntman directed Atomic Blonde
and Deadpool 2 and co-directed the first John

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:03.760
Wick.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:07.080
He's the perfect director to bring into the
franchise at this moment, and he's sure to

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:10.700
put his own frenetic, sardonic spin on the
series with Hobbs and Shaw.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:16.039
As you're probably well aware from having
watched and rewatched the trailers for Hobbs

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:19.700
and Shaw with your mouth swinging open in
awe, we've already seen a lot of action.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.780
But for those afraid that the promo clips
have given away the movie's best set pieces,

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:27.360
Chris Morgan is here to set those fears at
ease, telling Empire that there's more to

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:27.880
come:

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.780
"We have so much that we're holding back.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:32.340
This is a blink of the action in the film.

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:33.100
A blink.”

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.640
It's a gutsy claim to make, but a believable
one.

00:08:36.089 --> 00:08:39.340
After all, if you compare the trailers that
were released for Fate of the Furious with

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:43.680
the actual film, it's easy to see how the
promos barely scratched the surface.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:47.680
With so much action and story to tell, there's
also a fair chance that Hobbs and Shaw could

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:52.911
share a similar running time to Fate of the
Furious, which gave audiences an epic, 150-minute

00:08:52.911 --> 00:08:55.380
cinematic ride.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.270
If you're giddy at the prospect of Hobbs and
Shaw enjoying their own series of films rather

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:01.930
than just one standalone spinoff, you're in
luck.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:06.089
Leitch has confirmed that Hobbs and Shaw is
intended as the first movie of an ongoing

00:09:06.089 --> 00:09:07.089
franchise.

00:09:07.089 --> 00:09:08.449
The director told Collider:

00:09:08.449 --> 00:09:10.490
"We're starting a franchise.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:13.690
So we want it to be a little bit more grounded,
it's a little bit more character-centric.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.940
We're going to set up the stakes for these
guys and their relationship."

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:21.430
If that sounds a little slow for a Fast &amp; Furious
movie, you've got nothing to worry about.

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:27.290
"We're also going to have some great set pieces
and some action that you'd expect from that

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:31.029
type of franchise, you know, it's something
that opens in summer."

00:09:31.029 --> 00:09:35.709
Awesome though that may be, there is a downside:
It means that Hobbs and Shaw probably won't

00:09:35.709 --> 00:09:39.740
be starring in Fast and Furious 9 while their
own respective franchise gets going.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:44.980
The long-running Fast and Furious franchise
could be coming to an end after the next couple

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.110
of films, but it seems as though the saga's
creative team is already putting plans in

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:52.240
place to keep the series alive in new and
exciting ways.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:55.740
Hobbs and Shaw is the first of many planned
Fast and Furious spinoffs.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:10:00.120
On top of a theme park ride, Diesel has also
teased that a Fast and Furious movie with

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:01.980
a woman in the lead may be coming soon.

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:06.940
In an Instagram post shared at the beginning
of 2019, Diesel revealed that he and producer

00:10:06.959 --> 00:10:11.170
Samantha Vincent had heard a pitch at Universal
for just such a movie.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:14.130
Judging by his Instagram caption, it sounds
like it went well:

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:17.880
"There are three new spin offs that we have
promised Universal…this week we heard a

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:22.949
pitch for the Fast female protagonist driven
spinoff I created in 2017, and you can tell

00:10:22.949 --> 00:10:25.800
by the smile on Samantha's face it was VERY
exciting."

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.440
In the meantime, we'll just have to live like
Dom:

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:30.900
"I live my life a quarter-mile at a time."

